---
import AlternativesListLayout from '../../../layouts/AlternativesListLayout.astro';
import { SPLICE_ALTERNATIVES, SPLICE_CRITERIA, SAMPLE_COLUMNS, SPLICE_VERIFIED } from '../../../data/splice-alternatives';

const quickAnswer = `
  <p><strong>If the problem with Splice is that everyone has the same sounds, Sonura is the pick here:</strong>
  it creates a new one-shot, loop or vocal chop for your prompt instead of licensing you a copy from a shared
  library. If what you want is a bigger human-made catalogue, Output Arcade, LANDR Samples and Loopcloud are the
  closest swaps, and nothing below changes that.</p>
  <p>Ranked on whether you can release what you make without clearing anything, how many other producers have
  the same sound, and what it costs to start. Every entry says who should skip it, ours included.</p>
`;

const methodNote = `
  Every library here licenses the same file to every subscriber, which is how sample libraries work, so
  originality is judged on what you can do with a sound, not on download counts none of them publish. Pricing
  is given as a shape rather than a figure: it moves, and a stale number helps nobody. The links go to their own
  sites so you can check us.
`;

const stillRightBody = `
  <p>If you want the biggest human-made catalogue in one place, Splice is still the honest answer. It lists more
  than 3 million sounds, credits roll over from month to month, and every sound comes with a royalty-free licence
  for commercial use. It also bought Spitfire Audio in April 2025.</p>
  <p>What Splice does not give you is a sound of your own. The licence is non-exclusive, so the loop in your beat
  is available to every other subscriber, and there is no free tier beyond a cheaper first month.</p>
  <p>Plenty of producers use both: Splice for the staple sounds everyone expects, and a tool that creates new ones
  for the parts that need to be yours.</p>
`;

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'What is the best Splice alternative?',
    answer:
      'It depends on why you are leaving. For sounds nobody else has, Sonura, because it creates them for your prompt. For a library you can reshape as you play, Output Arcade. For the cheapest paid library, Loopcloud. For free, BandLab Sounds or the Sonura free plan.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is there a free Splice alternative?',
    answer:
      'Yes. The Sonura free plan creates samples with daily credits and no card, and free output is public domain (CC0). BandLab Sounds gives free samples with a free account. <a href="https://freesound.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-link">Freesound</a> is free too, but each sound carries its own Creative Commons licence, and some of them rule out commercial use.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Are Splice samples royalty-free?',
    answer:
      'Yes. Splice licenses every sound royalty-free for commercial use, but non-exclusively, so other subscribers can use the same sound. That is true of every library on this page.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Which Splice alternative gives me sounds nobody else has?',
    answer:
      'Only one entry on this list creates new audio rather than licensing a shared file: the <a href="/tools/ai-sample-generator/" class="text-link">Sonura AI sample generator</a>. On a paid plan what you create is exclusively yours. Output Arcade is the closest of the libraries, because you reshape its loops as you play them.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What about Tracklib?',
    answer:
      'Tracklib is for sampling real recorded songs, which none of the others offer. Those samples need a licence: you register the release and share income with the original artist. Its separate sounds library is royalty-free. It is a different job from the libraries above.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I use both Splice and Sonura?',
    answer:
      'Yes, and many producers do. Use Splice for staple sounds and Sonura for the one-shots, loops and vocal chops that need to be yours. Sonura also runs inside your DAW through the free <a href="/plugin/" class="text-link">Sonura Flow plugin</a>.',
  },
];

const sources = [
  { label: 'Splice plans: credits, rollover and catalogue size', url: 'https://splice.com/plans' },
  { label: 'Splice help centre: the royalty-free sample licence', url: 'https://intercom.help/splice-b7a2d5b83f2e/en/articles/8652642' },
  { label: 'MusicTech: Splice acquires Spitfire Audio, April 2025', url: 'https://musictech.com/news/industry/splice-acquires-spitfire-audio/' },
  { label: 'Output Arcade: plans, trial and licence', url: 'https://output.com/products/arcade' },
  { label: 'LANDR Samples', url: 'https://samples.landr.com/' },
  { label: 'Loopcloud plans', url: 'https://www.loopcloud.com/cloud/subscriptions/plans' },
  { label: 'BandLab Sounds', url: 'https://www.bandlab.com/sounds/home' },
  { label: 'Noiiz membership plans', url: 'https://www.noiiz.com/membership' },
  { label: 'ADSR Sounds', url: 'https://www.adsrsounds.com/' },
  { label: 'Tracklib pricing and sample clearance', url: 'https://www.tracklib.com/pricing' },
];
---

<AlternativesListLayout
  competitor="Splice"
  competitorSlug="splice-alternative"
  title="7 Best Splice Alternatives in 2026, Free and Paid | Sonura"
  description="Splice alternatives ranked on licence, originality and cost. Free and paid sample libraries compared, plus one that creates sounds nobody else has."
  keywords="splice alternative, splice alternatives, free splice alternative, best splice alternatives, splice alternatives free, alternative to splice, splice competitor, royalty free samples, ai sample generator"
  headline="Best Splice Alternatives in 2026"
  quickAnswer={quickAnswer}
  items={SPLICE_ALTERNATIVES}
  columns={SAMPLE_COLUMNS}
  verifiedOn={SPLICE_VERIFIED}
  methodNote={methodNote}
  criteria={SPLICE_CRITERIA}
  stillRightTitle="When Splice is still the right call"
  stillRightBody={stillRightBody}
  faqs={faqs}
  sources={sources}
  finalCtaTitle="Sounds nobody else has"
  finalCtaSubtitle="One-shots, loops and vocal chops created for your prompt, with stems on every plan. Free to start, no credit card."
  finalCtaButtonText="Start free"
/>
